IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ma-nouns`
IMPORT `ma-s02-damages`

-- Tests for ma-s02-damages.l4.  Every expected value is written from the text of s 2 before the run.
-- Argument order of each rule is the order of its GIVEN in ma-s02-damages.l4; JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING
-- are written out in full so that each line can be read against the text without looking up the rule.

§ `Tests -- s 2(1), the proviso "unless he proves"`

-- He must prove BOTH that he had reasonable ground to believe AND that he did believe up to the time the contract was made.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) he proves reasonable ground to believe and belief up to the time the contract was made` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not proved on either limb: this section gives no defence on these facts (JUST FALSE for that provision's defence only).
#ASSERT `s 2(1) he proves reasonable ground to believe and belief up to the time the contract was made` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) he proves reasonable ground to believe and belief up to the time the contract was made` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) he proves reasonable ground to believe and belief up to the time the contract was made` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A limb not given: one limb unproved already defeats the proviso; otherwise the text decides nothing.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) he proves reasonable ground to believe and belief up to the time the contract was made` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) he proves reasonable ground to believe and belief up to the time the contract was made` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) he proves reasonable ground to believe and belief up to the time the contract was made` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(1) he proves reasonable ground to believe and belief up to the time the contract was made` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(1) he proves reasonable ground to believe and belief up to the time the contract was made` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 2(1), liability though the misrepresentation was not fraudulent`

-- Arguments: entered into a contract after a misrepresentation by another party; loss as a result; would be liable had it been
-- fraudulent; proved reasonable ground; proved belief up to the time the contract was made.
-- All conditions met and nothing proved by way of the proviso: "that person shall be so liable".
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the person making the misrepresentation is liable to damages` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Only one limb of the proviso proved: the proviso is not met, so the liability stands.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the person making the misrepresentation is liable to damages` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the person making the misrepresentation is liable to damages` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Both limbs proved: "unless he proves ..." lifts the liability.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the person making the misrepresentation is liable to damages` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The "where" conditions and the "if" condition each fail on their own.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the person making the misrepresentation is liable to damages` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the person making the misrepresentation is liable to damages` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the person making the misrepresentation is liable to damages` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A fact not given: NOTHING, never FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the person making the misrepresentation is liable to damages` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the person making the misrepresentation is liable to damages` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the person making the misrepresentation is liable to damages` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The proviso not yet decided (the belief limb not given, the ground limb proved): NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the person making the misrepresentation is liable to damages` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- A limb of the proviso known unproved already means the proviso fails, whatever the other limb.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the person making the misrepresentation is liable to damages` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A no stands whatever else was not given: no loss.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the person making the misrepresentation is liable to damages` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The proviso proved lifts the liability whichever way the other facts fall.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the person making the misrepresentation is liable to damages` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- s 2(2), the matters the text says the opinion has regard to`

#ASSERT `s 2(2) the opinion was formed having regard to the three matters the text names` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the opinion was formed having regard to the three matters the text names` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the opinion was formed having regard to the three matters the text names` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the opinion was formed having regard to the three matters the text names` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the opinion was formed having regard to the three matters the text names` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the opinion was formed having regard to the three matters the text names` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the opinion was formed having regard to the three matters the text names` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 2(2), damages in lieu of rescission`

-- Arguments: entered into a contract after a misrepresentation; made otherwise than fraudulently; would be entitled to rescind;
-- claimed in proceedings that the contract ought to be or has been rescinded; who is deciding; of opinion that it would be
-- equitable; had regard to the nature of the misrepresentation; to the loss if the contract were upheld; to the loss rescission would cause.
-- Everything met, the court deciding: "the court or arbitrator may declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission".
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the court or arbitrator may declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `The court` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An arbitrator is named too.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the court or arbitrator may declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `An arbitrator` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Each "where" or "if" condition fails on its own: JUST FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the court or arbitrator may declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `The court` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the court or arbitrator may declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) `The court` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the court or arbitrator may declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) `The court` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the court or arbitrator may declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `The court` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A fraudulent misrepresentation fails the "Where ... otherwise than fraudulently" limb, in the same "Where" clause as the entitlement to rescind: JUST FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the court or arbitrator may declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `The court` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The same no stands over a not-covered limb: fraudulent AND the claim is before another body.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the court or arbitrator may declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `Another body` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- And over one matter not regarded.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the court or arbitrator may declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `The court` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- And over a fact not given: a known no on a limb the text joins with "and" wins.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the court or arbitrator may declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) `The court` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A body the text does not name: not covered, NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the court or arbitrator may declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `Another body` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The opinion not formed having regard to one of the three matters: not covered, NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the court or arbitrator may declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `The court` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the court or arbitrator may declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `The court` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A no from a "where" or "if" condition stands over a not-covered limb: fraudulent AND not claimed.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the court or arbitrator may declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) `The court` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A fact not given: NOTHING, never FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the court or arbitrator may declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `The court` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the court or arbitrator may declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `The court` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the court or arbitrator may declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `The court` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the court or arbitrator may declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `The court` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the court or arbitrator may declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `The court` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 2(2), the same permission as a regulative rule (traced, not asserted: a DEONTIC value cannot be compared in an #ASSERT on the main binary)`

-- Conditions met, the court acts: the permission is used and the rule is FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 2(2) the permission of the court or arbitrator to declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission` `The court` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `The court` DOES `declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission` AT 3
-- Conditions met, an arbitrator acts.
#TRACE `s 2(2) the permission of the court or arbitrator to declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission` `An arbitrator` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `An arbitrator` DOES `declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission` AT 3
-- Conditions met, nothing happens: the permission is still standing (a MAY has no time limit here: the text gives none).
#TRACE `s 2(2) the permission of the court or arbitrator to declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission` `The court` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
-- Conditions not met: there is no permission to exercise.
#TRACE `s 2(2) the permission of the court or arbitrator to declare the contract subsisting and award damages in lieu of rescission` `The court` (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH

§ `Tests -- s 2(3)`

-- Damages in lieu of rescission under (2) are available whether or not he is liable under (1): the answer is (2)'s, whatever (1) says.
#ASSERT `s 2(3) damages may be awarded under subsection (2) whether or not he is liable to damages under subsection (1)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) damages may be awarded under subsection (2) whether or not he is liable to damages under subsection (1)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) damages may be awarded under subsection (2) whether or not he is liable to damages under subsection (1)` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) damages may be awarded under subsection (2) whether or not he is liable to damages under subsection (1)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) damages may be awarded under subsection (2) whether or not he is liable to damages under subsection (1)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) damages may be awarded under subsection (2) whether or not he is liable to damages under subsection (1)` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(3) damages may be awarded under subsection (2) whether or not he is liable to damages under subsection (1)` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Where he is so liable, any award under (2) is taken into account.  Arguments: liable under (1); an award has been made under (2).
#ASSERT `s 2(3) an award under subsection (2) is to be taken into account in assessing his liability under subsection (1)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not liable under (1): the "where" condition fails.
#ASSERT `s 2(3) an award under subsection (2) is to be taken into account in assessing his liability under subsection (1)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) an award under subsection (2) is to be taken into account in assessing his liability under subsection (1)` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) an award under subsection (2) is to be taken into account in assessing his liability under subsection (1)` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Liable but no award made: no award to take into account; not covered.
#ASSERT `s 2(3) an award under subsection (2) is to be taken into account in assessing his liability under subsection (1)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(3) an award under subsection (2) is to be taken into account in assessing his liability under subsection (1)` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(3) an award under subsection (2) is to be taken into account in assessing his liability under subsection (1)` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(3) an award under subsection (2) is to be taken into account in assessing his liability under subsection (1)` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(3) an award under subsection (2) is to be taken into account in assessing his liability under subsection (1)` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- The amount to be taken into account is the amount of the award itself; the text says "taken into account", not "deducted".
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the amount of the award under subsection (2) that is to be taken into account` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST 500) EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the amount of the award under subsection (2) that is to be taken into account` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the amount of the award under subsection (2) that is to be taken into account` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST 500) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the amount of the award under subsection (2) that is to be taken into account` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST 500) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the amount of the award under subsection (2) that is to be taken into account` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST 500) EQUALS NOTHING
